            "id": "1607042846363877376",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Long story short—\n\nKnowledge compounds on itself, and enables you to perform more abstract thinking.\n\nYou're not going to 'run out of space', and deliberately trying to save space by not remembering is hampering your ability for higher order thought."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2022-12-25T15:57:26.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1607042846363877376"
        ],
        "id": "1607042846363877376",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 3,
          "impression_count": 10203,
          "like_count": 55,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 5
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1607042844182851584",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Memorizing actually allows for new conceptual understanding, it’s not just rote BS.\n\nAnd while there is some “wetware” limit based on the number of synapses, that limit is roughly the memory size of the movie of your entire life. It’s why some people can have photographic memory"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2022-12-25T15:57:26.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1607042844182851584"
